    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Haley and Knott give expressions for the eight other $ F_{2} $ marker genotypes, and values for other designs easily follow when the appropriate conditional probabilities are employed. This regression approach was independently suggested by Martínez and Curnow (1992) for the analysis of backcross populations. These authors also detail how missing marker information can be accommodated (Martínez and Curnow 1994a).",
      "source_page": 468,
      "printed_page": 448,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter15:p024:b8"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        119.0,
        602.0,
